NNAAMMEE
       bmptopnm - convert a BMP file into a PBM, PGM, or PNM image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       bbmmppttooppnnmm

       [--vveerrbboossee]

       [_b_m_p_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       bbmmppttooppnnmm reads a Microsoft Windows or OS/2 BMP file as input.  and pro‐
       duces a PBM, PGM, or PNM image as output.  If the input is  colormapped
       and  contains only black and white, the output is PBM.  If the input is
       colormapped and contains only black white and gray, the output is  PGM.
       Otherwise, the output is PPM.

       bbmmppttooppnnmm  understands  BMP  files  compressed  with run length encoding
       (RLE4/RLE8), but not if that encoding  includes  a  "delta"  (which  is
       rare).  bbmmppttooppnnmm recognizes the delta and issues an error message.

       Before  Netpbm  10.75 (June 2016), bbmmppttooppnnmm could not convert Version 4
       or Version 5 Windows BMP images.

       bbmmppttooppnnmm cannot convert BMP files compressed with JPEG or PNG encoding.
       It  recognizes  the  compression  and  issues an error message.  Before
       Netpbm 10.32 (February 2006), bbmmppttooppnnmm couldn't convert RLE8 BMP  files
       either,  and  before  Netpbm 10.85 (December 2018), it couldn't convert
       RLE4 (between 10.32 and 10.85, it would act like it recognized the for‐
       mat, but produce garbage output).

       Before  Netpbm  10.18  (September 2003), this program could not convert
       BMP images with the BI_BITFIELDS format ("compression type").  It would
       recognize the format and issue an error message.

       bbmmppttooppnnmm cannot convert OS/2 BMP files with 16 bits per pixel (only be‐
       cause the author did not have a complete specification for  them).   It
       recognizes the format and issues an error message.  Before Netpbm 10.16
       (June 2003), it also could not convert Windows BMP files with  16  bits
       per pixel.



